      "response": {
        "kind": "value",
        "value": {
          "content": "Here's a plan to address the user's request, ensuring all necessary steps are taken to obtain the missing documents for Case PA-100002:\n\n## Plan: Request Missing Documents for Case PA-100002\n\n**Objective:** Secure the clinical notes and imaging report for Case PA-100002 from the provider within 7 days to facilitate case review.\n\n**Key Stakeholders:**\n*   Reviewer/Case Manager (initiating the request)\n*   Provider (recipient of the request)\n\n---\n\n### Action Plan\n\n1.  **Prepare the Request Communication:**\n    *   Draft a clear and concise request to the provider.\n    *   Include all necessary details: Case ID, specific missing documents, deadline, and rationale (briefly).\n    *   Ensure the tone is professional and emphasizes the importance for case review.\n\n2.  **Send the Request:**\n    *   Utilize the standard communication channel for provider interactions (e.g., secure messaging portal, encrypted email, fax). *If not specified, assume the primary secure method for contacting providers.*\n    *   Send the request to the designated contact person/department for Case PA-100002.\n\n3.  **Document the Request:**\n    *   Log the date and time the request was sent in the case management system.\n    *   Note the specific documents requested and the 7-day deadline.\n    *   Attach a copy of the sent communication to the case file for record-keeping.\n\n4.  **Set a Follow-up Reminder:**\n    *   Set a calendar reminder for 5 days from the date of the initial request. This allows for a proactive reminder before the 7-day deadline expires.\n\n5.  **Monitor and Follow-up:**\n    *   If documents are not received by the 5-day mark, send a polite reminder to the provider, reiterating the deadline.\n    *   If documents are still not received by the 7-day deadline, initiate an escalation process (see step 7).\n\n6.  **Receive and Process Documents:**\n    *   Once the clinical notes and imaging report are received, promptly upload them to the correct case file (PA-100002).\n    *   Update the case status to reflect that all necessary documents have been received.\n    *   Notify the reviewer that the documents are now available.\n\n7.  **Escalation (if documents are not received within 7 days):**\n    *   Inform the immediate supervisor or case review lead about the delay.\n    *   Determine the next steps, which may include:\n        *   A more formal follow-up communication (e.g., a phone call in addition to written request).\n        *   Involving provider relations or a designated escalation team.\n        *   Assessing the impact on the case review timeline and adjusting expectations.\n\n---\n\n### Communication Template (for Step 1)\n\n**Subject:** Urgent Request for Missing Documents - Case ID: PA-100002\n\n**Body:**\n\nDear Provider,\n\nWe are currently conducting a comprehensive review of **Case PA-100002**. To ensure an accurate and timely decision, we require the following essential documents, which are currently missing from the case file:\n\n*   **Clinical Notes**\n*   **Imaging Report**\n\nThese documents are crucial for our reviewer to proceed with the case evaluation.\n\nPlease provide these missing documents within **7 calendar days** from the date of this request. Kindly submit them via [Specify preferred secure submission method, e.g., \"our secure provider portal,\" \"encrypted email to documents@example.com,\" \"fax to 555-123-4567\"].\n\nThank you for your prompt attention to this urgent matter. We appreciate your cooperation in facilitating the review process.\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Your Name/Reviewer Name]\n[Your Title/Department]\n[Organization Name]",
